      "mergeID": "63003decc8404844be941fd3",
      "mergedPostDetails": "I'm sure everyone can agree that the current interact buttons on the selfie camera are extremely clunky and in some cases impossible to use without contorting your body into credulous positions just to reach one button. \n\nThe implementation of ray cast interaction like the current menu system would make using the camera so much easier and quicker, with a pointer people could easily point to the button they desire without having to wave their hand around hoping to hit the button.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Ray cast Buttons For Selfie Camera",
      "parentID": "5c908c978ba2b5033a5c1fc3",
      "pinned": false,
      "postDeleted": false,
      "postID": "5baef83899affd09e3a5a102",
      "private": false,
      "reactions": null,
      "sourceLink": null,
      "spam": false,
      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5bbbf6aa17bab877dd8bc723|full_name}: I'm writing to you from the future. One year later, we now have Udon released. It's amazing. Unfortunately, nobody at VRChat headquarters bothered yet to send down an internee to the stream camera prefab laying in the basement to switch the buttons to raycast or colliders and disable the stupid controller rendering that are ruining every recording. It would be so easy, even I could do it. Meanwhile, the most frustrating feature in VRChat is still \"under review\", not even in \"planned\". I might write you another message from 2022 when we have raycasting in VRChat, but still the same unusable buttons from over 5 years ago.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
