      "internal": false,
      "mergeID": "63003e1b0ec0c844b3f46373",
      "mergedPostDetails": "I am using WMR headset and i found out the (stream) camera in VRChat is not easy to control. The small buttons are hard to touch.\n\nI discovered the default \"loading\" avatar has much larger fingers and i can see where i touch the button. Yes i can really touch it.\nBut if you use another loaded avatar, it's very possible it has another dimensions compared to default avatar design. \n\nThen i cannot see where i am exactly pointed... It's like grabbing small pin. I am more waving in air around to hope the correct button light up.\n\nI am thinking to add slight colored pointer beam so i can see where i am pointed at the camera. This is useful if you have non-body avatar like box which has no hands or arms. The slight colored beam will help you where you're pointed.\n\nGrabbing selfie stick is also unclear and hard where i am pointed. So add small beam as pointer. You can bind it to button of controller to enable beam pointer.",
      "mergedPostTitle": "Camera + WMR usage is not easy, hard to point.",
      "pinned": false,
      "postID": "5baef83899affd09e3a5a102",
